1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,515
Dry, rubbery chicken breast is the most
common dinner disappointment.

2
00:00:04,969 --> 00:00:07,870
It's lean meat that overcooks in minutes.

3
00:00:08,324 --> 00:00:10,996
But with seven simple steps, you can cook

4
00:00:11,006 --> 00:00:14,151
chicken breast that is tender, juicy and
safe,

5
00:00:14,326 --> 00:00:18,528
using just a pan, a little salt and a
thermometer.

6
00:00:18,889 --> 00:00:21,733
It takes about thirty minutes, start to
finish,

7
00:00:21,792 --> 00:00:24,577
plus what to do if it still comes out dry.

8
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:26,238
WikiTube.

9
00:00:26,413 --> 00:00:28,641
Whatever it is, here's how.

10
00:00:28,933 --> 00:00:31,941
Chicken breast has very little fat, so
there

11
00:00:31,951 --> 00:00:33,785
isn't much margin for error.

12
00:00:34,448 --> 00:00:37,152
Two things cause most of the dryness.

13
00:00:37,698 --> 00:00:40,997
Uneven thickness, where the thin end
overcooks while

14
00:00:41,007 --> 00:00:43,424
the thick end is still raw, and cooking

15
00:00:43,434 --> 00:00:44,675
it for too long.

16
00:00:45,639 --> 00:00:46,799
We'll fix both.

17
00:00:47,253 --> 00:00:49,345
We'll also use a quick salt brine for

18
00:00:49,355 --> 00:00:52,317
extra moisture, and a thermometer, which
is the

19
00:00:52,327 --> 00:00:55,623
only reliable way to know when chicken is
done.

20
00:00:56,170 --> 00:00:57,377
Let's get started.

21
00:00:57,923 --> 00:01:00,337
Even if you have never cooked chicken
before,

22
00:01:00,396 --> 00:01:01,579
you can do this.

23
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:04,981
It simply takes attention at the right
moments.

24
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:06,658
Here's what you need.

25
00:01:07,019 --> 00:01:09,828
Two or three boneless chicken breasts.

26
00:01:10,003 --> 00:01:11,534
Coarse salt and pepper.

27
00:01:11,825 --> 00:01:13,369
A skillet with a lid.

28
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:16,387
A little oil with a high smoke point.

29
00:01:16,678 --> 00:01:20,555
A meat mallet, or a rolling pin or heavy
pan.

30
00:01:21,357 --> 00:01:23,783
And an instant-read meat thermometer.

31
00:01:24,329 --> 00:01:26,583
If you only buy one new kitchen tool

32
00:01:26,593 --> 00:01:29,123
this year, make it that thermometer.

33
00:01:29,786 --> 00:01:32,667
Nothing here is expensive, and most of it

34
00:01:32,677 --> 00:01:34,661
is already in your kitchen.

35
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,232
Step one.

36
00:01:36,779 --> 00:01:39,334
Place the chicken breast between two
sheets of

37
00:01:39,344 --> 00:01:42,629
plastic wrap or baking paper on a cutting
board.

38
00:01:43,594 --> 00:01:46,150
Using a mallet, a rolling pin or the

39
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:48,959
bottom of a heavy pan, gently pound the

40
00:01:48,969 --> 00:01:51,548
thickest part until the whole breast is
about

41
00:01:51,558 --> 00:01:55,528
three quarters of an inch, or two
centimetres, thick.

42
00:01:56,493 --> 00:01:58,828
Don't pound it into a pancake, because you

43
00:01:58,838 --> 00:02:00,590
just want an even shape.

44
00:02:00,951 --> 00:02:03,506
Equal thickness means the whole piece
cooks at

45
00:02:03,516 --> 00:02:07,393
the same speed, which is the key to juicy
results.

46
00:02:08,543 --> 00:02:10,844
Very large breasts can also be cut in

47
00:02:10,854 --> 00:02:15,474
half horizontally to make two thinner
cutlets, which cook faster.

48
00:02:16,033 --> 00:02:17,077
Step two.

49
00:02:17,368 --> 00:02:20,815
Dissolve two tablespoons of salt in four
cups,

50
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:23,428
or one litre, of cold water.

51
00:02:24,230 --> 00:02:26,379
Put the chicken in the water, and leave

52
00:02:26,389 --> 00:02:28,444
it for thirty minutes in the fridge.

53
00:02:29,246 --> 00:02:31,325
The salt helps the meat hold on to

54
00:02:31,335 --> 00:02:33,401
more moisture while it cooks.

55
00:02:34,064 --> 00:02:36,619
If you're short of time, skip the brine,

56
00:02:36,629 --> 00:02:39,928
and instead salt the chicken generously on
both

57
00:02:39,938 --> 00:02:42,468
sides fifteen minutes before cooking.

58
00:02:43,619 --> 00:02:45,942
Don't brine for more than an hour, or

59
00:02:45,952 --> 00:02:47,832
the texture can turn spongy.

60
00:02:48,495 --> 00:02:51,350
Raw chicken must always stay in the
fridge.

61
00:02:52,013 --> 00:02:54,255
Always use a clean bowl and wash it

62
00:02:54,265 --> 00:02:57,506
afterward with hot soapy water, since raw
chicken

63
00:02:57,516 --> 00:02:59,558
juices carry bacteria.

64
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:01,121
Step three.

65
00:03:01,354 --> 00:03:03,666
Remove the chicken from the brine and pat

66
00:03:03,676 --> 00:03:06,171
it very dry with paper towels.

67
00:03:06,973 --> 00:03:09,933
Dry meat browns, wet meat steams.

68
00:03:10,735 --> 00:03:13,337
Don't rinse raw chicken under the tap,
because

69
00:03:13,347 --> 00:03:16,109
that splashes bacteria around your sink.

70
00:03:16,656 --> 00:03:19,337
Brush each side with a teaspoon of oil,

71
00:03:19,361 --> 00:03:23,586
and season with pepper, paprika, garlic
powder

72
00:03:23,715 --> 00:03:25,827
or any dry spices you like.

73
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:29,565
If you skipped the brine, add salt now.

74
00:03:30,367 --> 00:03:32,505
Wash your hands and the board with hot

75
00:03:32,515 --> 00:03:34,151
soapy water afterward.

76
00:03:34,953 --> 00:03:38,763
Smoked paprika, garlic powder and dried
thyme make

77
00:03:38,773 --> 00:03:41,863
an easy all-purpose rub, with no sugar to

78
00:03:41,873 --> 00:03:43,253
burn in the pan.

79
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:44,879
Step four.

80
00:03:45,333 --> 00:03:47,993
Heat a skillet over medium-high heat for
two

81
00:03:48,003 --> 00:03:50,916
minutes, then add a thin layer of oil.

82
00:03:51,463 --> 00:03:53,542
When it shimmers, lay the chicken in the

83
00:03:53,552 --> 00:03:56,175
pan, presentation side down.

84
00:03:56,629 --> 00:03:58,788
It should sizzle right away.

85
00:03:59,752 --> 00:04:02,087
Leave it alone for five to six minutes

86
00:04:02,097 --> 00:04:04,978
without moving it, until the underside is
a

87
00:04:04,988 --> 00:04:06,647
deep golden brown.

88
00:04:07,612 --> 00:04:09,062
Don't crowd the pan.

89
00:04:09,423 --> 00:04:12,975
If you're cooking more than two breasts,
work in batches.

90
00:04:13,428 --> 00:04:16,423
That browned crust is where the flavor
comes from.

91
00:04:16,970 --> 00:04:20,521
If the pan smokes heavily, lower the heat
slightly.

92
00:04:20,975 --> 00:04:25,049
A deep golden color is what you want, not
black.

93
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,598
Step five.

94
00:04:26,959 --> 00:04:29,515
Flip the chicken with tongs, then turn the

95
00:04:29,525 --> 00:04:32,522
heat down to medium-low and cover the pan

96
00:04:32,532 --> 00:04:33,448
with a lid.

97
00:04:34,412 --> 00:04:37,618
The trapped steam finishes the cooking
gently, so

98
00:04:37,628 --> 00:04:40,600
the center cooks through without the
outside burning.

99
00:04:41,146 --> 00:04:45,545
Cook for another five to seven minutes,
depending on thickness.

100
00:04:46,092 --> 00:04:49,481
Don't keep lifting the lid, because the
heat escapes.

101
00:04:50,283 --> 00:04:53,129
A gentle finish is the difference between
juicy

102
00:04:53,139 --> 00:04:55,834
and dry chicken, so be patient and keep

103
00:04:55,844 --> 00:04:56,865
the heat low.

104
00:04:57,319 --> 00:04:59,666
If your breasts are very thin, three to

105
00:04:59,676 --> 00:05:02,995
four minutes will be enough, so start
checking early.

106
00:05:03,533 --> 00:05:04,589
Step six.

107
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:05,947
Don't guess.

108
00:05:06,749 --> 00:05:09,804
Push an instant-read thermometer into the
thickest part

109
00:05:09,814 --> 00:05:12,600
of the breast, without touching the pan.

110
00:05:13,564 --> 00:05:16,585
Chicken is safe to eat at 165 degrees

111
00:05:16,595 --> 00:05:19,485
Fahrenheit, or 74 Celsius.

112
00:05:19,938 --> 00:05:21,740
Take the chicken out of the pan once

113
00:05:21,750 --> 00:05:24,642
it reaches that temperature, because it
keeps cooking

114
00:05:24,652 --> 00:05:26,242
a little as it rests.

115
00:05:26,904 --> 00:05:30,807
If it's below 165, cover the pan, and

116
00:05:30,817 --> 00:05:33,997
cook for a minute or two more, then check
again.

117
00:05:34,962 --> 00:05:37,829
Cutting into it to look is not reliable,

118
00:05:37,923 --> 00:05:40,011
and it lets the juices escape.

119
00:05:40,813 --> 00:05:42,870
Check a second breast as well if you

120
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:45,680
are cooking several, because they never
finish at

121
00:05:45,690 --> 00:05:47,616
exactly the same time.

122
00:05:48,167 --> 00:05:49,408
Step seven.

123
00:05:50,558 --> 00:05:52,731
Move the chicken to a clean board or

124
00:05:52,741 --> 00:05:56,791
plate, and let it rest for five to ten
minutes.

125
00:05:57,942 --> 00:06:00,672
The juices relax and spread back through
the

126
00:06:00,682 --> 00:06:03,537
meat, instead of running out when you cut.

127
00:06:04,339 --> 00:06:07,124
Cover loosely with foil if your kitchen is
cool.

128
00:06:07,578 --> 00:06:10,575
Then slice across the grain, in slices
about

129
00:06:10,585 --> 00:06:11,780
half an inch thick.

130
00:06:12,744 --> 00:06:16,540
Serve in a salad, a sandwich or with
vegetables.

131
00:06:17,690 --> 00:06:20,580
Store leftovers in the fridge within two
hours,

132
00:06:20,639 --> 00:06:23,030
and eat within three to four days.

133
00:06:23,483 --> 00:06:25,551
Try the sliced chicken over a salad or

134
00:06:25,561 --> 00:06:28,858
inside a wrap for an easy lunch the next
day.

135
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:31,410
If the chicken came out dry, you can

136
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:32,546
still save dinner.

137
00:06:32,906 --> 00:06:35,311
Slice it thinly, and warm it for a

138
00:06:35,321 --> 00:06:36,574
minute in broth.

139
00:06:36,866 --> 00:06:39,465
You can also shred it for tacos or soup.

140
00:06:39,826 --> 00:06:42,449
If the center is pink, do not guess.

141
00:06:42,810 --> 00:06:45,308
Pink can be safe, and white can be

142
00:06:45,318 --> 00:06:48,103
raw, so trust only the thermometer.

143
00:06:48,905 --> 00:06:52,796
If it reads below 165 degrees Fahrenheit,
return

144
00:06:52,806 --> 00:06:53,885
it to the pan.

145
00:06:54,433 --> 00:06:57,230
A thermometer is only useful if it is
accurate.

146
00:06:57,464 --> 00:06:59,448
Test it in a glass of ice water:

147
00:06:59,681 --> 00:07:05,021
it should read 32 degrees Fahrenheit, or 0
Celsius.

148
00:07:05,568 --> 00:07:07,773
If it is off by a few degrees,

149
00:07:07,797 --> 00:07:10,780
adjust it if you can, or replace it.

150
00:07:11,442 --> 00:07:14,416
Slide the tip into the thickest part, away

151
00:07:14,426 --> 00:07:15,389
from the pan.

152
00:07:16,051 --> 00:07:18,198
Wait until the number stops moving.

153
00:07:19,163 --> 00:07:23,051
Wash the probe with hot soapy water after
each use.

154
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,016
Spread the chicken in a shallow container
so

155
00:07:26,026 --> 00:07:29,531
it cools quickly, then cover it and
refrigerate.

156
00:07:29,985 --> 00:07:32,878
For longer storage, freeze it, and thaw it

157
00:07:32,888 --> 00:07:35,755
overnight in the fridge, never on the
counter.

158
00:07:36,417 --> 00:07:39,391
Reheat leftovers until they are steaming
hot all

159
00:07:39,401 --> 00:07:43,615
the way through, or 165 degrees Fahrenheit
again.

160
00:07:44,277 --> 00:07:46,717
Add a splash of water or broth, and

161
00:07:46,727 --> 00:07:50,081
cover the dish, so the meat stays tender.

162
00:07:50,633 --> 00:07:52,861
Here are the mistakes to avoid.

163
00:07:53,663 --> 00:07:57,018
First, cooking a thick, uneven breast.

164
00:07:58,168 --> 00:08:00,422
The thin part dries out before the thick

165
00:08:00,432 --> 00:08:01,580
part is safe.

166
00:08:01,941 --> 00:08:03,763
Even it out first.

167
00:08:04,913 --> 00:08:07,652
Second, cooking without a thermometer.

168
00:08:08,315 --> 00:08:10,894
Overcooking by only a few minutes can ruin

169
00:08:10,904 --> 00:08:14,258
the texture, and undercooking is unsafe.

170
00:08:14,549 --> 00:08:17,393
And third, slicing right away.

171
00:08:18,056 --> 00:08:20,783
Resting keeps the juices where they
belong.

172
00:08:21,933 --> 00:08:24,675
Do these three things right, and your
chicken

173
00:08:24,685 --> 00:08:26,402
will be tender every time.

174
00:08:26,763 --> 00:08:31,278
Keep it simple, trust the thermometer, and
enjoy the result.

175
00:08:31,833 --> 00:08:32,993
Let's recap.

176
00:08:34,143 --> 00:08:35,698
Even out the thickness.

177
00:08:36,059 --> 00:08:37,579
Brine for moisture.

178
00:08:38,729 --> 00:08:40,505
Dry and season well.

179
00:08:41,052 --> 00:08:42,781
Sear in a hot pan.

180
00:08:43,931 --> 00:08:46,740
Flip, cover and lower the heat.

181
00:08:47,704 --> 00:08:51,534
Check with a thermometer for 165 degrees.

182
00:08:51,988 --> 00:08:55,087
And rest the chicken, then slice across
the grain.

183
00:08:56,052 --> 00:08:59,467
Seven steps, about thirty minutes of
cooking, and

184
00:08:59,477 --> 00:09:01,542
chicken breast that stays juicy.

185
00:09:02,693 --> 00:09:06,303
Bonus sections cover rescuing dry or pink
chicken,

186
00:09:06,478 --> 00:09:10,761
checking your thermometer, and storing
leftovers safely.

187
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:14,457
That's how you cook chicken breast without
drying it out.

188
00:09:14,818 --> 00:09:18,393
If dinner was juicy tonight, subscribe to
WikiTube,

189
00:09:18,452 --> 00:09:21,981
because we publish a new how-to every
single day.

190
00:09:22,434 --> 00:09:24,247
Tell us in the comments how you season

191
00:09:24,257 --> 00:09:26,349
your chicken, and what you would like us

192
00:09:26,359 --> 00:09:28,064
to explain next.

193
00:09:29,215 --> 00:09:30,305
See you tomorrow.

194
00:09:30,968 --> 00:09:34,348
Next time, try different spices, because
the method

195
00:09:34,358 --> 00:09:36,528
stays exactly the same.

196
00:09:36,633 --> 00:09:37,805
That's WikiTube.

197
00:09:38,038 --> 00:09:40,313
Whatever it is, here's how.
